      "figure": "fig-40",
      "conclusion": "PASS",
      "blockers": [],
      "observations": [
        "Independently observed exactly two complete nested circular outlines, N wholly inside Z and offset upper-left, N backslash-hatched, Z minus N unhatched, and N/Z labels in the correct regions. The prepared 640-by-640 native raster preserves all of these facts without clipping or boundary contact.",
        "Source inventory maps to fig-40-z-source-boundary / fig-40-z-set and fig-40-n-source-boundary / fig-40-n-set. Each boundary has 96 pointOnCircle assertions; every N boundary vertex has an inside-Z assertion. Actual spec has 2 polygons, 20 hatch segments and 2 text labels, not semantic member points.",
        "fig-40-n-source-hatching maps twenty deterministic segments with connects, displacement and endpoint-inside assertions. In user space the displayed backslash has positive dx and negative dy because SVG screen y is inverted. The actual raster confirms descending-right strokes, wholly within N except deliberate label clearance.",
        "fig-40-z-source-label and fig-40-n-source-label bind the text objects and inside-region assertions; Z additionally has an outside-N distance assertion. SVG text reads only Z at screen (475,370) and N at (284,258), each 48px, matching the actual visible labels.",
        "The complement is the unhatched region inside Z but outside N, not the exterior of Z. No explicit nonpositive examples, numerical member labels, or written exercise solutions have been added. The taught relation N subset Z is instructional prose, not an answer-key annotation.",
        "No source arrow, visible point marker, instructional grid, ticks, axes, extra subfigure or values are present or missing. connects uses its arrow field to identify a hatch segment, not a directed arrow. Hidden SVG construction ellipses and unused hidden paths are not source member points or extra visible objects.",
        "Visible SVG ink, muted hatching and paper use semantic CSS variables. Hidden JSXGraph construction nodes retain nonvisible renderer-default orange paint; this is not a visible figure color or cultural content. The actual neutral native raster is clean, nonblack, readable and unobscured.",
        "Modern additions are explicitly separated in the spec: 96-vertex circle regularization, exact layout coordinates/radii, 18px hatch spacing, inset/clearance choices and centered 48px typography. They are not source measurements or counted source elements.",
        "Current official draft/render receipts are successful and hash-bound to this spec/SVG; the native-raster receipt binds this exact SVG to the observed native PNG. No validator, renderer or native producer was rerun for this comparison."
      ],
      "independentPixelInventory": [
        "One complete thick outer circular outline; one complete smaller inner circular outline, wholly inside and offset toward the upper left. Neither circle intersects the other, and there is visible positive clearance all around.",
        "Only the smaller disk is hatched. Its strokes descend toward the right on the screen (northwest to southeast, backslash direction). The larger disk outside the smaller disk is unhatched.",
        "N is centered in the smaller disk, with a local light opening around the letter. Z is in the unhatched outer-minus-inner region toward the lower right. These are set labels, not member points.",
        "No Q, arrow, semantic point marker, axis, grid, given numeral, extra subfigure, or answer-bearing annotation. A tiny stray dark scan mark outside the main outer boundary at the upper-left image edge has no mathematical role.",
        "The unhatched part inside Z is Z minus N; the exterior of the outer circle is not that complement. This agrees with the modern text's positive-integer N convention and nonpositive-integer complement."
