      "observations": [
        "Independently observed exactly three complete nested circular outlines, N wholly inside Z wholly inside Q. Z is lower/right within Q and N upper/left within Z. Source and actual native640 output agree on strict containment with visible clearance and complete unclipped boundaries.",
        "The N disk is backslash-hatched; Z minus N is slash-hatched; Q minus Z is unhatched. The actual raster retains the opposite hatch directions and correct region separation without cross-hatching N or shading Q minus Z.",
        "Source boundaries map to fig-41-q-source-boundary / fig-41-q-set, fig-41-z-source-boundary / fig-41-z-set and fig-41-n-source-boundary / fig-41-n-set. Each has 96 pointOnCircle assertions. The source-bound nested vertices have inside-Q / inside-Z assertions, rather than boundary counts alone.",
        "Spec has 3 circular polygons, 35 Z-ring hatch segments, 15 N-disk hatch segments and 3 text objects. fig-41-z-source-hatching maps connects/displacement/inside and inner-child-exclusion distance assertions; fig-41-n-source-hatching maps connects/displacement/inside assertions. The apparent many SVG ellipses are hidden construction vertices/endpoints, not a source point population.",
        "Q, Z and N are in their respective regions with label clearance. SVG contains only Q at screen (490,186), Z at (425,418), N at (324,318), each 48px. The viewed native640 confirms their complete readable footprints do not meet the boundaries or hatches.",
        "The three-level inclusion and both complements match complete modern prose using positive-integer N, integer Z and rational Q. No numerical member examples, derived exercise answers, new equivalences or answer-bearing annotations are present.",
        "No source arrow, grid, number line, axis, tick, measured value or second panel is omitted. Hatch connects fields do not imply arrowheads; the source and actual native have no directed arrows.",
        "Visible SVG paint uses semantic ink/muted/paper roles and the actual neutral PNG is clean, nonblack and unclipped. Nonvisible renderer-default construction paint is not a visible theme choice. No copied Cyrillic/Chinese figure text, handwriting, flags, historical symbols or cultural fiction.",
        "Spec descriptions separate exact radii/coordinates, 96-vertex circle regularization, 18px hatch spacing, inset/label gaps and 48px typography from source facts. These are modern layout choices; the source supplies topology, label regions and hatch direction, not metric values or an exact hatch count.",
        "Current successful author validation/render/native receipts bind the observed SVG and PNG to the frozen spec. Assertions were inspected as text and existing evidence reused; no standalone validation, renderer or native producer was rerun."
      ],
      "independentPixelInventory": [
        "Exactly three complete closed circular outlines, strictly nested. The largest Q circle surrounds an intermediate Z circle offset downward and somewhat right; the smallest N circle lies above-left of the Z center and wholly inside Z. All nested boundaries have visible positive clearance.",
        "The smallest N disk has northwest-to-southeast (backslash) hatching. The region inside Z but outside N has southwest-to-northeast (slash) hatching. The region inside Q but outside Z is unhatched.",
        "N sits in the smallest disk; Z sits in the intermediate-minus-smallest region toward the lower right; Q sits in the largest-minus-intermediate region toward the upper right. Light openings keep the labels separate from hatch strokes.",
        "No directed arrow, semantic member point, axis, instructional grid, given numeral, extra panel, or answer annotation. The hatch strokes are region textures, not a counted population.",
        "The diagram expresses N strictly inside Z strictly inside Q, retaining Z minus N and Q minus Z as separate regions. It is not three disjoint sets or three overlapping but noncontained circles."
      ],
